"""The fixed 64-byte cache-line representation used by the impulse engine.

The inline byte storage is little-endian and contains all scalar state, eight
indexed axon targets, and arena links. The axon array begins at the same byte
offset as the former eight scalar fields, so snapshots remain compatible.
"""
open pack Minicolumn {
    erg storage: Array[u8, 64];
    layout little;
    fields {
        erg charge: u8 at 0;
        erg threshold: u8 at 8;
        erg myelination: u8 at 16;
        erg idle_ticks: u8 at 24;
        erg flags: u8 at 32;
        erg payload: u8 at 40;
        erg layer_depth: u16 at 48;
        erg coincidence_low: u64 at 64;
        erg coincidence_high: u64 at 128;
        erg axons: Array[u32, 8] at 192;
        erg free_list_link: u32 at 448;
        erg inhibitory_link: u32 at 480;
    }
}

"""One bounded input event presented to the impulse engine.

`mask_low` and `mask_high` form the 128-bit coincidence mask. `energy` is an
integer marker carried by the event; no floating-point state is introduced.
"""
open struct Wavefront {
    erg mask_low: u64,
    erg mask_high: u64,
    erg energy: u8,
}

"""Contiguous arena state with an O(1) free-list for minicolumn slots.

The arena owns every column and the free-list links. `free_list_head` points
to the next reusable slot, while `active_count` tracks allocated columns.
"""
open struct CorticalFabric[N: Usize] {
    erg columns: Array[Minicolumn, N],
    erg free_list_head: u32,
    erg active_count: u32,
}

"""Return the fixed width of one minicolumn in bytes.

The result is both the serialized column width and the intended cache-line
size. The operation has no allocation, mutation, or failure path.
"""
open verb minicolumn_size_bytes() -> u32 {
    return 64u32;
}
